@@ -21,3 +21,19 @@ are provided by the existing joystick and Unitree node implementations.
 The entry no longer uses verification flags, controller freshness gates, a
 fault state, or the `--cold-start-debug-joints` option. Agent model/data checks
 still apply. There is no separate stand policy in this entry.
+
+### Observation timing for newly trained RobotLab VAE policies
+
+Before producing action `a_t`, the 96-dimensional actor frame `O_t` contains
+the current robot state, velocity command, and last executed raw action
+`a_(t-1)`. The VAE receives `[O_(t-4), O_(t-3), O_(t-2), O_(t-1), O_t]`,
+flattened to 480 dimensions, with consecutive frames sampled every 20 ms.
+Both training and deployment clear history once at reset and initially fill
+all five slots with the first frame.
+
+During training, the encoder's state estimate and latent code feed a decoder
+that predicts `O_(t+1)`. Transitions ending an episode are excluded from this
+prediction loss so reset poses are not used as future targets. The actor uses
+`O_t`, the current code, and visual features; deployment does not run the decoder.
+Retrain and export matching ONNX files after changing the history semantics;
+older policies trained with an extra action delay require their matching input layout.
